wo connections so  $3,400 a month and then of course with a  four nine server redundancy you're  doubling that again 478 that's six to  eight hundred dollars a month the other  on the partner interconnect it's a  sliding scale it starts about $39 a  month for an it 50 megabit attachment  and goes all the way up to $1700 for a  10 gig attachment our pairing solutions  are free both carrier our direct peering  solutions free our carriers peering  solution is free of course you may have  to be paying some money to ever the  carrier is that's helping you appear but  we have a settlement free peering  solution of course you do pay egress  costs on those links and those aggress  costs on our internet egress cost rate  so speaking of egress on an on VPN on  VPN it's just like an internet  connection so depending on how you're  connecting to us and where you're  connecting to us that's runs from about  8 cents a gig all the way to 23 cents a  gig and the higher end of the scale is  for places like you know Australia and  South America where costs us a lot more  to provide transit of those locations  for dedicated and partner interconnect  in North America we charge two cents per  gig if you're interested in other  locales please go to the website and all  that pricing is available there as well  for carrier and direct peering we do  give a discount on our standard internet  rate of egress and in North America  that's five cents per gig for both  carrier and dedicated and direct peering  so we gave a lot of sessions at this  conference and this is the list of all  the sessions that are here the reason  I'm putting this up is all these  sessions will be available on youtube so  if you miss something that's a crucial  interest to you like I think there's  actually one happening exactly the same  time so if you were worrying about  enterprise-ready networking for gke  which is happening at exactly the same  time slot go to youtube and you'll be  able to get that presentation online and  finally two final things I I don't know  if you guys have seen this we have a  wonderful poster that's a it's an online  giveaway in other words you go to this  site and either you can download it  yourself or you can have it mailed to  you but this is a poster that shows our  network all our pop locations all our  data center locations all our undersea  cables all our terrestrial cabling etc  all in one beautiful picture so it's  kind of a cool you know put up on your  wall and people will ask you what's the  map of the world all about finally in  closing I like if you could please give  feedback on this session you'll find  feedback in the next 18 application  under let's see if I get this right  under notifications and they'll have all  the sessions that you've attended and  you can get feedback there it's kind of  hard to find but we really appreciate  any feedback you can give  [Music]

